From 10ef5cd456c926dd70186dca9340061f3e21516d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arthur Heymans <arthur@aheymans.xyz>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:40:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] drivers/efi/capsules: Do not coalesce capsules into
 reserved RAM

The capsule memory map takes every cacheable resource as RAM, including
reserved RAM ranges such as TSEG. With TSEG on QEMU q35, which sits
above CBMEM in a reserved RAM resource, the coalescing buffer lands in
SMRAM: ramstage writes there are dropped once TSEG is enabled and the
payload reads back garbage.

Add the reserved resources on top, as bootmem does.

TEST=CrabEFI runtime-image-test with CRABEFI_PAYLOAD_MM=1 on QEMU q35
(SMM in TSEG): capsules are coalesced below CBMEM and consumed.

Signed-off-by: Arthur Heymans <arthur@aheymans.xyz>
---
 src/drivers/efi/capsules.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/drivers/efi/capsules.c b/src/drivers/efi/capsules.c
index c53e1b0246..0d2769200d 100644
--- a/src/drivers/efi/capsules.c
+++ b/src/drivers/efi/capsules.c
@@ -722,6 +722,9 @@ void efi_parse_capsules(void)
 		       IORESOURCE_ASSIGNED | IORESOURCE_CACHEABLE, IORESOURCE_MEM |
 		       IORESOURCE_FIXED | IORESOURCE_STORED | IORESOURCE_ASSIGNED |
 		       IORESOURCE_CACHEABLE, BM_MEM_RAM);
+	/* Like bootmem: reserved RAM (e.g. TSEG) is not usable for capsules. */
+	memranges_add_resources(&memory_map, IORESOURCE_RESERVE, IORESOURCE_RESERVE,
+				BM_MEM_RESERVED);
 
 	if (ENV_X86_32)
 		init_pae_pagetables(&pae_page_tables);
